SUMMARY:UC OSPO All-Campus Virtual Meetup: Ten Years of Browser Nano Exten
 sions   Show and Tell
LOCATION:Online
DESCRIPTION:Join the UC OSPO Network for an all-campus hybrid meetup featu
 ring Neal Fultz\, statistical consultant for UCLA Social Sciences\, as he 
 looks back on ten years of building browser extensions. It started after t
 he Anthem data breach. The result is a set of six nano extensions\, each u
 nder 100 lines of code\, that run in Firefox and Chrome-based browsers.\n\
 nFultz will explain why he built them and how. He will also cover how the 
 browser extension ecosystem differs from other open source communities. A 
 Show and Tell follows the talk.\n\nThis event is hybrid. Choose one:\n\nIn
  person: 11690L\, Young Research Library (YRL). No registration needed. Ju
 st come.\nOn Zoom: register using the registration link. Registration is r
 equired for Zoom only\n\nHosted by UCLA Library's Tim Dennis and Leigh Pha
 n. Zoom meeting managed by the UC OSPO Network.\n\nView all upcoming UC OS
 PO Network events.
